// @emit-error emitProgram: bare null needs a struct-typed context
// BOUNDARY PIN: the one value-shaped node class that does NOT discard as a statement.
// `null` has no rep of its own — its lowering is chosen by the type of the slot it flows
// into (a `ref.null` of some heap type, an i32 sentinel, or a null-tagged union box), and a
// discarded statement supplies no slot. So it rejects while every other class in
// `discarded-expression-statement-classes.vl` drops, and the message says what is missing
// rather than calling the statement unsupported.
function f() {
  null
  0
}
print(f())
